        "In short: the UAE Ministry of Education curriculum is the public-school pathway taken mainly by Emirati nationals and taught largely in Arabic, IGCSE is a set of externally examined subject qualifications usually sat at 16 inside a British-curriculum private school, and the IB is a broader, internationally recognised continuum culminating in the Diploma at 18. Most fee-paying private schools in the UAE run IGCSE, the IB, or both, rather than the national curriculum, which mainly serves government schools and a smaller number of private schools targeting Emirati families directly.",
