        "Yes, in both directions, but Emirati and Arab-national students applying to UAE public universities need one extra step that expatriate families sending children to universities abroad usually do not: a Ministry of Education equivalency certificate confirming that a foreign or private-school qualification is equivalent to the UAE's own secondary certificate. Without it, government universities such as UAE University, Zayed University and the Higher Colleges of Technology, along with government scholarships, are generally unavailable, even to a student holding a strong IB score or set of A Levels.",
